# Ignore everything
*

# Allow Rust source
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates/
!crates/**

# cfgd-core embeds these repo-root example manifests via include_str! at
# compile time, so every image that builds a cfgd-core-dependent binary needs
# them in the build context.
!examples/
!examples/**

# Allow build files
!Dockerfile
!Dockerfile.*

# Allow pre-built binaries (release Docker builds)
!binaries/
!binaries/**

# Allow tests
!tests/
!tests/**

# Allow README for labels
!README.md

# Allow only the demo container's staged binary, not the whole demo/ tree:
# `demo/Dockerfile` is read directly by `docker build -f` and never needs
# this file, and `task docker:cli`/`task docker:operator` build from this
# same repo-root context — an unqualified `!demo/` would let every future
# demo asset (the recorded init.tape, the multi-megabyte GIF) leak into
# those unrelated builds too. demo/bin/cfgd (a host-built binary staged
# there before `docker build` — see demo/Dockerfile for why it isn't copied
# straight out of target/) is the only thing those builds actually need.
!demo/bin/
!demo/bin/**

# Re-ignore build artifacts inside allowed dirs
target/
